   "stem": "One of the points of intersection of the curves $y = 1 + 3x - 2x^{2}$ and $y = \\frac{1}{x}$ is $\\left(\\frac{1}{2}, 2\\right)$. Let the area of the region enclosed by these curves be $\\frac{1}{24}\\left(\\ell\\sqrt{5} + m\\right) - n\\log_{e}\\left(1+\\sqrt{5}\\right)$, where $\\ell, m, n \\in \\mathbb{N}$. Then $\\ell + m + n$ is equal to",
